# =====================================================================
# Release V059 -- wire the referential-integrity gate into orchestration
# =====================================================================
# Registers the V058 RI gate (Audit.usp_Check_Referential_Integrity) as a POST-RUN job so
# Orchestrate_Build fires it AFTER every load and a violating build cannot reach PBI.
#
# It is NOT a DAG job: the new category POSTRUN_GATE keeps it OUT of the dependency waves
# (Orchestrate_Build CELL 4 excludes that category), and the notebook runs it explicitly
# after the waves (new CELL 9b) via Audit.ETL_Run_Process -- so it self-logs to
# Audit.Process_Execution_Log (SUCCEEDED = integrity OK ; FAILED = the SP THROWs on any
# orphaned fact fk / missing dim -1 sentinel). A FAILED gate skips the semantic-model
# refresh and fails the run.
#
#   * Audit.Process_Category.Data.sql -- adds POSTRUN_GATE (+ GOLD_AGG, previously unseeded).
#   * Audit.Process_Config.Data.sql   -- adds POSTRUN_RI_CHECK -> Audit.usp_Check_Referential_Integrity.
#
# BOTH files are idempotent (DELETE + reseed), so this redeploys the full seed.
#
# NOTEBOOK (deploys SEPARATELY via the Fabric pipeline, NOT this manifest): re-import
# Fabric/Notebooks/Orchestrate_Build.ipynb -- it now excludes POSTRUN_GATE from the waves
# (CELL 4) and fires the gate post-build (CELL 9b). The .py mirror is updated to match.
#
# Run: .\Scripts\Deploy.ps1 -Manifest Releases\V059__wire_ri_gate_orchestration.manifest -SkipTests
# =====================================================================

DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Category.Data.sql
DEPLOY  Fabric\Audit.Process_Config.Data.sql

TEST
